{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 sending 0xa5 never asserted recv_buf_valid, so reg_dat_do stayed ~0 instead of 0xa5 and TB hit TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received with FAIL 0xdead. CONE_SLICE is unresolved (0/1, only picosoc/spiflash.v:52 and scripts/quartus/system.v:67 etc.) with no simpleuart recv logic, so trace wins. Root cause in picosoc/simpleuart.v:39 where reg [3:1] recv_state truncates the receiver to 3 bits and prevents the full start+8data+stop sequence from completing.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@
 	reg [31:0] cfg_divider;

-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
 	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;", "expected": "tohost PASS with byte 0xa5 received, no TRAP: uart timeout (vs FAIL 0xdead)"}

